sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/altitude-coupling> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Demand rises and supply falls with height together, so the flyable heights reach down to the ground (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "In an atmosphere where air density and oxygen partial pressure both fall with height, the minimum speed of lift-supported flight and the power to fly at it rise with height while the aerobic supply falls, so flight possible at a height is possible at every lower height, infeasibility propagates upward, and a design that cannot fly at the ground cannot fly at any height. The direction is proved; the size of the effect is data and it is gentle." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Favored.lean) as an extension of the neutral case of Kimura (1962) to non-opposing selection; no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "h1 ≤ h2 and feasible(h2) implies feasible(h1); not feasible(0) implies not feasible(h) for all h ≥ 0" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **The minimum speed rises with height.** -/
theorem vmin_mono {W S CL : ℝ} (hW : 0 < W) (hS : 0 < S) (hCL : 0 < CL) {h₁ h₂ : ℝ} (h : h₁ ≤ h₂) :
    vminAt A W S CL h₁ ≤ vminAt A W S CL h₂"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Altitude.Atmosphere" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Altitude.vmin_mono", "Delphi.Altitude.demand_mono", "Delphi.Altitude.supply_anti", "Delphi.Altitude.feasible_downward_closed", "Delphi.Altitude.ceiling", "Delphi.Altitude.infeasible_at_ground_infeasible_everywhere" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "The DIRECTION of the effect is proved; its SIZE is data and it is gentle (about 30% more required capacity from 0 to 5000 m, arterial content 0.190 to 0.173 ml/ml), and the real fish sits more than thirty times below every boundary at every height. So nothing here supports reading \"the feasible region shrinks with altitude\" as the reason a fish cannot fly high: the reason is the oxygen budget at sea level. Compensation an animal might make at altitude (haematocrit, ventilation, cardiac output) is held fixed, and no bird data is used." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Altitude.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/altitude-coupling> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/altitude-coupling> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-altitude-coupling> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-altitude-coupling> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Altitude.vmin_mono with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 0 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 23.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Altitude.lean (152 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Altitude.vmin_mono, Delphi.Altitude.demand_mono, Delphi.Altitude.supply_anti, Delphi.Altitude.feasible_downward_closed, Delphi.Altitude.ceiling, Delphi.Altitude.infeasible_at_ground_infeasible_everywhere: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:58:20.213Z): 0 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler:  Controls: 16 of 16 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/altitude-coupling> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

